<% --[[ What a navigation gets back: the part of the document that changed, and nothing else.

        The shell is already on screen, so sending it again would mean rebuilding a bar that is
        correct, throwing away its blur surface and replaying its entrance on every click. That is
        exactly what made the hub feel like a site rather than an application.

        Only two things about the shell depend on the page. Both come back marked out of band, which
        is the same mechanism the tray counters and the toasts already use: htmx lifts them out of
        the response and puts them where their id already is, then swaps what is left into `#view`.

        The title is a plain element on purpose. htmx reads it out of the fragment and puts it on the
        document, so the window keeps naming the page you are actually on. ]] %>
<title><%= title %></title>

<div id="view"><%- body %></div>

<%- render("nav", { nav = nav, oob = true }) %>
<div id="toasts" aria-live="polite" hx-swap-oob="true"><%- toasts or "" %></div>
